-- title:
--   χ(U_q)=± 1 at a prime q ∥ N with ρ̄ ramified
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic $0$, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal O)$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V=2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho\colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to \mathrm{End}_k(V)$ which is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline k$ has no invariant submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $N\ge 1$ be such that the $\mathbb C$-span of the $\mathbb Z$-lattice of weight-$2$ level-$\Gamma_0(N)$ cusp forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is everything, and let $S_0\subseteq S$ be finite sets of naturals with every element of $S$ prime, $p\in S$, every prime divisor of $N$ lying in $S$ and no prime divisor of $N$ lying in $S_0$. Let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T=\mathbb{T}_{N,2,S_0}$ — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$ — to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $P$ acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta'(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a further such discrete valuation ring, finite as an $\mathcal O$-module via a local algebra structure map, and let $\chi\colon \mathbb T\to\mathcal O'$ be a ring homomorphism whose reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O'}$ is $\theta'$ followed by the induced map of residue fields $k\to\mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal O')$. Finally let $q$ be a prime with $q\ne p$, $q\mid N$, $q^2\nmid N$, and suppose $\bar\rho$ is not unramified at $q$, i.e. some valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $q$ as a non-unit and some $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ satisfy $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)\ne 1$. Then there is an integer $a$ with $a=1$ or $a=-1$ such that $\chi(U_q)=a$ in $\mathcal O'$.
--
--   This is the statement that a characteristic-zero point of the Hecke algebra congruent to a ramified absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$ has Atkin–Lehner eigenvalue $\pm 1$ at a prime exactly dividing the level, in particular that $\chi(U_q)$ is a unit; classically it combines level lowering at $q$ with the $a_q^2=1$ relation for newforms of level divisible exactly once by $q$. It is used in the identification of the residue of $U_q$ with the trace of Frobenius on inertia coinvariants and in the corresponding statement about the local Hecke algebra.
